# Golden-clip regression - Phase 2.
#
# A fixed clip is run through the complete pipeline and its CSI curve compared
# against a recorded expected trajectory within tolerance.
#
# This is what makes the Crowd Stability Index testable at all. Without it,
# "the CSI looks right" is a judgement made once, by one person, on one clip -
# and any later change to a weight or a normalisation silently invalidates it.
#
# It works because frame timestamps derive from seq/fps rather than the wall
# clock: an unpaced offline run produces the identical curve the live
# demonstration produces (see VideoFileSource).
#
# Run this before freezing the CSI weights, and again after any change to
# them. Never tune weights during a rehearsal.
